# NestedText v3 - DTD switch mechanisms (measured 2026-09-16)
# Third of the deferred study notes (dodeka: marked sections + percent-p/s).
# Ordinal: hepta, next in the dtd-variants family.

marked-sections:
    > <![INCLUDE[ ... ]]> parses, <![IGNORE[ ... ]]> skips: the DTD's own
    > conditional compilation, sections toggled by parameter entity value.
    > SVG ships prefw and postfw IGNORE by default with TWO named slots;
    > a profile flips a slot and the framework re-reads. Switching is
    > declaration, never editing: the ignored text stays in the file.

percent-p-s:
    > %p 'xs:' plus %s ':xs' redefinable in the consumer's INTERNAL
    > SUBSET: the namespace prefix is a parameter, not a spelling. A
    > consumer renames the prefix without touching the grammar, which is
    > the driver-file override shape LAW.ASK.11 states for rounds. The
    > wild's own first-declaration-binds, measured in XMLSchema.dtd.

release-binding:
    > Stream 4 (depth as precedence): marked sections are the DTD-native
    > override slots beside prefw/postfw; every override the release
    > declares cites a slot, never a race. Stream 3 (forms): %p/%s is
    > why schematic spellings live in entities, never in prose.
